From 118416f8f1b3f98e0fce06b473b823e8e063995a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 02:03:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix #25234 - Add PowerPC thread state support to the XNU
 debugger ##debug

- Read and write GPRs via PPC_THREAD_STATE or PPC_THREAD_STATE64 by dbg bits
- Always call thread_get_state, convert only when the SDK provides it
- Single-step via MSR[SE] in srr1, ppc has no debug state flavor
- Enable the Mach exception port path and exc_msg codes on ppc (#25144)
- Fix ppc register aliases and add a ppc64 register profile
- Match `__POWERPC__` in the native plugin, gcc does not define `__powerpc__` on Darwin

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
